---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "The Yelp Hub: a working library on Yelp advertising"
description: "A maintained library on Yelp advertising for service businesses, from a Yelp Ads Certified Partner. What we learn managing real campaigns, written down."
permalink: /yelp/index.html

# The hub's own figure. Page-level keys, the same two an article card uses, so
# there is one convention for a feature image rather than one per slot.
# A bare filename resolved through site.cdn: see src/_data/site.js.
image: cs-img-trellis-1-portrait.webp
imagealt: A trellis, structure built before growth
imagecaption: Structure first, then growth
preloadImage: cs-img-trellis-1-portrait.webp

# The hub's own currency, not any article's. Nothing recomputes this: it says
# when a person last read the page for accuracy, which no build step can know.
reviewed: July 2026

intro:
  eyebrow: About the program
  headlineBefore: A working library on
  headlineAccent: Yelp advertising
  headlineAfter: for service businesses.
  lede: >-
    The Yelp Hub is a purposeful knowledge resource on Yelp advertising, built
    and maintained by Circulation Studio, a Yelp Ads Certified Partner since
    the program began. What we learn managing real campaigns gets written down
    here so you can check our thinking. Read it, cite it, or bring it to your
    next budget conversation.
  currency: >-
    Added to as the work produces something worth writing down, rather than on
    a schedule.
  building: >-
    Calculators and estimators are in the build phase and will be listed here
    when the first one ships.

# The certification proof. In the intro rather than the Start here band, where
# the comp draws it, because the band renders only when a piece declares
# itself and the page would otherwise ship without it.
badge:
  file: yelp/yelp-ads-partner-badge.png
  alt: Yelp Advertising Certified Partner
  label: Certified Partner

# The band's furniture only. The entry itself is an article carrying
# `starthere: true`, never a title and summary retyped here.
starthere:
  label: Start here

# Furniture only. Every card on the shelf is an article carrying a rank.
browse:
  eyebrow: Worth reading
  note: Chosen rather than sorted
  featureCta: Read the whitepaper

# Furniture only. Every entry is an article, grouped by its declared cluster.
map:
  title: The full index
  subtitle: Coverage map, everything published, by cluster
  meta: Seven clusters
  lede: >-
    For the reader who wants the whole picture rather than a recommendation.
    The subject laid out as seven clusters. Every long entry we have published
    sits under the cluster it belongs to. The library is added to as the work
    produces something worth writing down, so a cluster with one entry today
    is a cluster we are still in.
  pendingState: In preparation
  pendingNote: The longer entries for this cluster are in preparation.

# The one service offer on this page. The report rows are a SAMPLE, labelled as
# one in the note beneath them, not a real client's positions.
rank:
  eyebrow: Service, from the studio
  title: Yelp Rank Tracking
  body: >-
    Monthly tracking of where your business ranks in Yelp search for the terms
    that bring you work, reported plainly and tied to what we would change
    next. A managed service, run by the team, not a self-serve tool.
  cta: Ask about rank tracking
  reportTitle: Position report
  reportDate: 2026-06-30
  rows:
    - term: emergency plumber, Laguna Beach
      position: 3
      delta: Was 7
      moved: true
    - term: water heater repair
      position: 5
      delta: Held
      moved: false
    - term: drain cleaning near me
      position: 2
      delta: Was 4
      moved: true
    - term: slab leak detection
      position: 9
      delta: Was 14
      moved: true
  note: >-
    Sample rows from a monthly report. A real one carries your terms, your
    market and a note on what we would change next.
---
{% from "components/container.njk" import container %}
{% from "components/button.njk" import button %}

{#
  The Yelp Hub landing page.

  NOT AN ARTICLE, and deliberately outside src/yelp/. That directory's
  11tydata.js makes every file in it an article: article layout, /yelp/<slug>/
  permalink. The hub is neither, so it sits at src root like the five
  marketing pages and declares its own permalink, exactly as what-we-do.njk
  does. Keeping it out also keeps collections.yelp honest, since that
  collection is the hub's own data source and a hub listing itself would be a
  loop.

  PAGE RHYTHM IS 96px BETWEEN SECTIONS, not the section() macro's 96 top plus
  96 bottom, which would put 192 between them. That is the comp's rhythm and
  the comp is the authority on spacing. It is declared once as
  .cs-hub-section rather than written per section, so the rhythm is still in
  one place. See yelp-hub.css, which records the conflict with design.md
  section 4.
#}

{% call container(class="cs-hub-crumbs") %}
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <ol class="cs-hub-crumbs__list">
      <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
      <li aria-current="page">Yelp Hub</li>
    </ol>
  </nav>
{% endcall %}

{% call container(class="cs-hub-intro cs-hub-section cs-hub-section--first") %}
  <div>
    <p class="cs-eyebrow">{{ intro.eyebrow }}</p>

    <h1 class="cs-hub-intro__headline">
      {{ intro.headlineBefore }} <span class="cs-hub-intro__accent">{{ intro.headlineAccent }}</span> {{ intro.headlineAfter }}
    </h1>

    <p class="cs-hub-intro__lede">{{ intro.lede }}</p>

    {#- The currency line carries the review date beside it, because a claim
        about how current a library is means nothing without the date it was
        last checked. -#}
    <p class="cs-hub-intro__currency">{{ intro.currency }} Last reviewed {{ reviewed }}.</p>

    <p class="cs-hub-intro__building">{{ intro.building }}</p>
  </div>

  {#- The figure is decorative in the sense that the page reads without it,
      but it carries meaning per design.md section 10, so it takes real alt
      text rather than an empty attribute. Width and height are the slot's,
      not the file's: the card owns its dimensions. -#}
  <div class="cs-hub-intro__aside">
    <figure class="cs-hub-intro__figure">
      <img src="{{ site.cdn }}{{ image }}"
           alt="{{ imagealt }}"
           width="240" height="340" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
      <figcaption class="cs-eyebrow">{{ imagecaption }}</figcaption>
    </figure>

    {#- THE BADGE IS HERE AND THE COMP PUTS IT IN THE START HERE BAND. Moved
        because that band renders only when a piece carries `starthere`, and
        nothing does, so on the comp's placement the page would ship with no
        certification proof at all. The intro is where the claim is made in
        prose, so it is where the proof belongs. -#}
    <p class="cs-hub-badge">
      <img src="{{ site.cdn }}{{ badge.file }}"
           alt="{{ badge.alt }}"
           width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <span class="cs-hub-badge__label">{{ badge.label }}</span>
    </p>
  </div>
{% endcall %}

{#- START HERE. One piece, flagged on the piece itself rather than copied into
    this file, so a retitle cannot leave the band describing an older name. The
    band is omitted entirely when nothing carries the flag: an empty band with
    a placeholder row would read as a real recommendation. See YELP_STARTHERE
    in eleventy.config.js. -#}
{%- for entry in collections.yelpStartHere %}
{% call container(class="cs-hub-section") %}
  <a class="cs-starthere" href="{{ entry.url }}">
    <span class="cs-starthere__label">{{ starthere.label }}</span>
    <span>
      <span class="cs-starthere__title">{{ entry.data.title }}</span>
      <span class="cs-starthere__summary">{{ entry.data.summary }}</span>
    </span>
  </a>
{% endcall %}
{%- endfor %}

{#- BROWSE LAYER. Ranks 1 to 5 off the pieces themselves. Each group renders
    only if it has entries, so a one-piece shelf is a feature card alone
    rather than a feature card beside two empty columns. See SHELF_SLOTS. -#}
{%- set feature = collections.yelpShelf | shelfSlice(1, 1) | first %}
{%- set side = collections.yelpShelf | shelfSlice(2, 3) %}
{%- set row = collections.yelpShelf | shelfSlice(4, 5) %}
{%- if feature %}
{% call container(class="cs-hub-section") %}
  <div class="cs-browse__head">
    <p class="cs-eyebrow">{{ browse.eyebrow }}</p>
    <p class="cs-browse__note">{{ browse.note }}</p>
  </div>

  {#- The grid collapses to one column when nothing is beside the feature.
      No placeholder cards: an empty side column would read as a shelf that
      lost its contents. -#}
  <div class="cs-browse__top{{ " cs-browse__top--alone" if not side.length }}">
    <a class="cs-browse__feature" href="{{ feature.url }}">
      <img class="cs-browse__feature-img"
           src="{{ site.cdn }}{{ feature.data.image }}"
           alt="{{ feature.data.imagealt }}"
           width="642" height="320" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <span class="cs-browse__feature-body">
        <span class="cs-browse__feature-type">{{ feature.data.kind | kindLabel }}</span>
        <span class="cs-browse__feature-title">{{ feature.data.title }}</span>
        <span class="cs-browse__feature-summary">{{ feature.data.deck }}</span>
        <span class="cs-browse__spacer"></span>
        <span class="cs-browse__feature-meta">Updated {{ feature.data.updated | monthYear }}</span>
        <span class="cs-browse__feature-cta">{{ browse.featureCta }} <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></span>
      </span>
    </a>

    {%- if side.length %}
    <div class="cs-browse__side">
      {%- for entry in side %}
      <a class="cs-browse__card" href="{{ entry.url }}">
        <img src="{{ site.cdn }}{{ entry.data.image }}"
             alt="{{ entry.data.imagealt }}"
             width="440" height="170" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <span class="cs-hub-type{{ " cs-hub-type--lead" if entry.data.kind == "whitepaper" }}">{{ entry.data.kind | kindLabel }}</span>
        <span class="cs-browse__card-title">{{ entry.data.title }}</span>
        <span class="cs-browse__card-summary">{{ entry.data.summary }}</span>
      </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>

  {%- if row.length %}
  <div class="cs-browse__bottom">
    {%- for entry in row %}
    <a class="cs-browse__row" href="{{ entry.url }}">
      <img src="{{ site.cdn }}{{ entry.data.image }}"
           alt="{{ entry.data.imagealt }}"
           width="132" height="110" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <span>
        <span class="cs-hub-type{{ " cs-hub-type--lead" if entry.data.kind == "whitepaper" }}">{{ entry.data.kind | kindLabel }}</span>
        <span class="cs-browse__row-title">{{ entry.data.title }}</span>
        <span class="cs-browse__row-summary">{{ entry.data.summary }}</span>
      </span>
    </a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
{% endcall %}
{%- endif %}

{#- COVERAGE MAP. All seven clusters, always, whether or not anything has been
    published under them. The map's claim is that this is the whole subject,
    so dropping an empty cluster would shrink the subject to whatever happens
    to be written. See the yelpMap collection. -#}
{% call container(class="cs-hub-section") %}
  <div class="cs-map__head">
    <div>
      <h2 class="cs-map__title">{{ map.title }}</h2>
      <p class="cs-eyebrow">{{ map.subtitle }}</p>
    </div>
    <p class="cs-map__meta">{{ map.meta }}</p>
  </div>
  <p class="cs-map__lede">{{ map.lede }}</p>

  <div class="cs-map">
    {%- for cluster in collections.yelpMap %}
    <div class="cs-map__cluster">
      <div class="cs-map__cluster-head">
        <h3 class="cs-map__cluster-name" id="{{ cluster.slug }}">{{ cluster.name }}</h3>
        <p class="cs-map__cluster-state">
          {%- if cluster.lastAdded %}Last added {{ cluster.lastAdded | monthYear }}{% else %}{{ map.pendingState }}{% endif -%}
        </p>
      </div>

      {%- if cluster.entries.length %}
      <div class="cs-map__entries">
        {%- for entry in cluster.entries %}
        <a class="cs-map__entry" href="{{ entry.url }}">
          <span class="cs-hub-type cs-map__entry-type{{ " cs-hub-type--lead" if entry.data.kind == "whitepaper" }}">{{ entry.data.kind | kindLabel }}</span>
          <span>
            <span class="cs-map__entry-title{{ " cs-map__entry-title--lead" if loop.first }}">{{ entry.data.title }}</span>
            {%- if loop.first %}<span class="cs-map__entry-summary">{{ entry.data.summary }}</span>{% endif %}
          </span>
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      {%- else %}
      {#- The comp's empty row reads "Answered in the FAQ while the longer
          entries are in preparation", which claims an FAQ that does not exist
          yet. Reworded to something true today. -#}
      <p class="cs-map__pending">{{ map.pendingNote }}</p>
      {%- endif %}

      {#- No questions, no link. A cluster reading "0 questions in the FAQ"
          pointing at an anchor on a page nobody has built is worse than
          silence, for a reader and for a crawler. Counted, never declared. -#}
      {%- if cluster.faqCount %}
      <a class="cs-map__faq" href="/yelp/faq/#{{ cluster.slug }}">{{ cluster.faqCount }} {{ "question" if cluster.faqCount == 1 else "questions" }} in the FAQ <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
{% endcall %}

{#- RANK TRACKING. The one service offer on the page. The report card holds
    SAMPLE rows, said so in the note beneath them, because a real client's
    positions are not ours to publish. -#}
{% call container(class="cs-hub-section") %}
  <div class="cs-rank">
    <div>
      <p class="cs-rank__eyebrow">{{ rank.eyebrow }}</p>
      <h2 class="cs-rank__title">{{ rank.title }}</h2>
      <p class="cs-rank__body">{{ rank.body }}</p>
      {{ button(rank.cta, href="/contact/", class="cs-rank__cta") }}
    </div>

    {#- A table, because it is one: four rows of term, position and movement.
        The comp draws it as divs, which reads identically and tells a screen
        reader nothing about the columns. -#}
    <table class="cs-rank__report">
      <caption class="cs-rank__report-head">
        <span class="cs-rank__report-title">{{ rank.reportTitle }}</span>
        <span class="cs-rank__report-date">{{ rank.reportDate | monthYear }}</span>
      </caption>
      <thead class="sr-only">
        <tr><th scope="col">Search term</th><th scope="col">Position</th><th scope="col">Change</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for row in rank.rows %}
        <tr>
          <td class="cs-rank__term">{{ row.term }}</td>
          <td class="cs-rank__position">{{ row.position }}</td>
          <td class="cs-rank__delta{{ " cs-rank__delta--moved" if row.moved }}">{{ row.delta }}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
      {#- The note is inside the card, where the comp puts it, so it travels
          with the numbers it qualifies. A tfoot rather than a p, because a p
          cannot live in a table and the qualifier belongs to the table. -#}
      <tfoot>
        <tr><td class="cs-rank__note" colspan="3">{{ rank.note }}</td></tr>
      </tfoot>
    </table>
  </div>
{% endcall %}
